<article class="env-proposition" id="02YM">
<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/02YM">Proposition <span data-tag="02YM">7.3.1.16</span>.</a> Suppose we are given a diagram </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix@R =50pt@C=50pt{ &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\ar [dr]^{G} \ar@ {=&gt;}[]+&lt;0pt,-25pt&gt;;+&lt;0pt,-50pt&gt;^-{\alpha } &amp;  \\ K \ar [ur]^{\delta } \ar [rr]_{G_0} &amp;  &amp;  \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}} \]
</div>
<p> as in Definition <a data-tag="02Y9" href="/tag/02Y9">7.3.1.2</a>, where $\delta $ factors as a composition $K \xrightarrow { \gamma } \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\xrightarrow {F} \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}$ for some $\infty $-category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. Then: </p>
<p><dl>
<dt>$(1)$</dt>
<dd><p>
If $F$ is fully faithful and $\alpha $ exhibits $G$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\delta $, then it also exhibits $G \circ F$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\gamma $. 
</p>
</dd>
<dt>$(2)$</dt>
<dd><p>
If $F$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories and $\alpha $ exhibits $G \circ F$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\gamma $, then it also exhibits $G$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\delta $. 
</p>
</dd>
</dl></p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
<p>
<strong>Proof.</strong>
      Suppose that $F$ is fully faithful. Then, for every pair of objects $X,Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, the functor $F$ induces a homotopy equivalence of left-pinched morphism spaces 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{X/} \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} \{ Y\}  = \operatorname{Hom}^{\mathrm{L}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}}( X,X') \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}^{\mathrm{L}}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}}( F(X), F(Y) ) = \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ F(X) / } \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \{  F(Y) \}  \]
</div>
<p>
       Allowing $Y$ to vary and applying Corollary <a data-tag="028C" href="/tag/028C">5.1.7.16</a>, we see that the natural map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{X/} \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ F(X)/ } \times _{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ is an equivalence of left fibrations over $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. It follows that the induced map $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}_{X/} \times _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}} K \rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}_{ F(X) / } \times _{ \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} K$ is an equivalence of left fibrations over $K$. In particular it is a categorical equivalence of simplicial sets (Proposition <a data-tag="0285" href="/tag/0285">5.1.7.5</a>) and therefore left cofinal (Corollary <a data-tag="02NC" href="/tag/02NC">7.2.1.13</a>). Applying Corollary <a data-tag="02XR" href="/tag/02XR">7.2.2.3</a>, we see if $\alpha $ satisfies condition $( \ast _{F(X) })$ of Definition <a data-tag="02Y9" href="/tag/02Y9">7.3.1.2</a>, then it also satisfies condition $(\ast _ X)$. Assertion $(1)$ now follows by allowing the object $X$ to vary. 
    <p>
      We now prove $(2)$. Assume that $F$ is an equivalence of $\infty $-categories and that $\alpha $ exhibits $G \circ F$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\gamma $. Let $E: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a homotopy inverse of $F$. Then $E$ is left adjoint to $F$, so we can choose natural transformations 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \eta : \operatorname{id}_{ \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \rightarrow F \circ E \quad \quad \epsilon : E \circ F \rightarrow \operatorname{id}_{\operatorname{\mathcal{D}}} \]
</div>
<p>
       which are compatible up to homotopy in the sense of Definition <a data-tag="02EK" href="/tag/02EK">6.2.1.1</a>. Note that $\eta $ and $\epsilon $ are isomorphisms (Proposition <a data-tag="02DE" href="/tag/02DE">6.1.4.1</a>). Let $\alpha '$ denote a composition of the natural transformations 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  G \circ F \circ E \circ F \circ \gamma \xrightarrow {\epsilon } G \circ F \circ \gamma \xrightarrow {\alpha } G_0. \]
</div>
<p>
       Using Corollary <a data-tag="06ME" href="/tag/06ME">7.3.1.15</a>, we see that $\alpha '$ exhibits $G \circ F$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $E \circ F \circ \gamma = E \circ \delta $. Applying assertion $(1)$ to the fully faithful functor $E: \operatorname{\mathcal{D}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, we deduce that $\alpha '$ also exhibits $\delta $ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $G \circ F \circ E$. The compatibility of $\eta $ and $\epsilon $ guarantees that $\alpha $ is a composition of the natural transformations 
    <p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  G \circ \delta \xrightarrow { \eta } G \circ F \circ E \circ \delta \xrightarrow { \alpha ' } G_0. \]
</div>
<p>
       Applying Remark <a data-tag="02YJ" href="/tag/02YJ">7.3.1.12</a>, we conclude that $\alpha $ also exhibits $G$ as a right Kan extension of $G_0$ along $\delta $, as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
</p>
